# Profile two-column layout

`ProfilePage` uses a `lg:grid-cols-2` story order with **fixed anchors** and a
small **balancing tail**. Do not auto-pack every panel by height — that made
the page unreadable. Only the tail panels (`TAIL` in `ProfilePage.tsx`:
Extra-curriculars, then Links) may cross to the shorter column, measured
after render; the anchors below never move.

## Required order

| Left (anchors) | Right (anchors) | Tail (either column, shorter one wins) |
|------|--------|--------|
| Identity | Experience | Extra-curriculars |
| Addresses | Certifications | Links |
| Education | | |

## When you add a panel

1. Personal / location / school → **left**, under Identity (Addresses stays
   directly under Identity). Education rows use a leading school logo mark
   (like Experience’s company logo) so the two stacks feel balanced.
2. Career / credentials / extras → **right**, under Experience in a sensible
   sequence (certs before extracurriculars before links).
3. A new low-priority panel can join `TAIL` (append = lowest priority). Anything
   people read first stays an anchor.

## Avoid

- Measure-and-pack / masonry that moves *anchor* panels between columns
- Dumping every new section under Identity on the left
- Balancing Settings with this rule unless it shares the same panel pattern
